evidence.quote:
Across 54 ratings, the pooled mean was 4.65 ± 0.80, with 93% of ratings ≥ 4;
Metric means were 4.6 (reasoning), 4.5 (citation), and 4.8 (utility), and raters agreed within
one point on 85% of paired ratings.

With the PGG
the population grows faster and peaks higher, at around 3,200 agents against 2,400 without it;
the difference is statistically significant during this early phase.
